      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] This commit message bundles two independent logical changes (joined by `\" and \"` in the subject line and `\"In addition, ...\"` in the body) and narrates low-level symbol names (`REGION_CODE_RAM`, `REGION_CODE_RAM2`, `CONFIG_ROLLBACK_MPU_PROTECT`, `REGION_STORAGE`, `HOOK_SYSJUMP`) rather than focusing on high-level behavior and motivation:\n\n1. **Keeping the MPU enabled in `system_disable_jump()` when write-protect is unlocked** while gating sticky `ram_lock` configuration on `system_is_locked()` and disabling the MPU before sysjump.\n2. **Marking unused SRAM in the 256 MB code RAM aperture XN and inaccessible** via a background MPU region underneath the active code RAM region when `CONFIG_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` is enabled.\n\nPlease split this CL into two focused commits so each change can be reviewed, tested, and reverted independently.\n\n### Suggested commit messages if split into 2 CLs\n\n**CL 1 (Keep MPU enabled when unlocked):**\n```text\ncortex-m: Keep MPU enabled when write protect is unlocked\n\nPreviously, system_disable_jump() skipped all MPU and RAM lock\nconfiguration whenever the system was unlocked, leaving the MPU disabled\nafter jumping to RW on unlocked devices.\n\nAlways configure and enable the MPU in system_disable_jump() regardless\nof write-protect state so memory protections match production behavior\nwhen unlocked. Gate sticky hardware RAM lock configuration on\nsystem_is_locked() and disable the MPU before sysjump so unlocked\nsystems can still jump between images without requiring a reset.\n\nBUG\u003db:478947725\nTEST\u003dmake run-system\nTEST\u003d./test/run_device_tests.py -b bloonchipper -t mpu -t panic\n```\n\n**CL 2 (Mark unused code RAM XN and inaccessible):**\n```text\ncortex-m: Mark unused code SRAM XN and inaccessible\n\nOn chips with external storage that execute code from SRAM, the MPU\npreviously configured read-only executable access for the active code\nregion while leaving the rest of the 256 MB code RAM aperture with\ndefault background permissions.\n\nConfigure a lower-priority MPU region covering the 256 MB code RAM\naperture as execute-never (XN) with no access permissions, allowing the\nhigher-priority active code region to grant read and execute access\nonly to in-use code RAM.\n\nBUG\u003db:478947725\nTEST\u003dmake run-system\nTEST\u003d./test/run_device_tests.py -b bloonchipper -t mpu -t panic\n```\n\n### Suggested commit message if kept as a single CL\n\n```text\ncortex-m: Enable MPU when unlocked and restrict unused code SRAM\n\nPreviously, system_disable_jump() skipped all MPU and RAM lock\nconfiguration whenever the system was unlocked, and chips executing from\ncode SRAM left unused portions of the 256 MB code RAM aperture with\ndefault background permissions.\n\nAlways configure and enable the MPU in system_disable_jump() regardless\nof write-protect state, while gating sticky RAM lock configuration on\nsystem_is_locked() and disabling the MPU before sysjump so unlocked\nsystems can still jump between images. Additionally, configure a\nlower-priority MPU region covering the 256 MB code RAM aperture as\nexecute-never (XN) with no access permissions so only the active code\nregion remains readable and executable.\n\nBUG\u003db:478947725\nTEST\u003dmake run-system\nTEST\u003d./test/run_device_tests.py -b bloonchipper -t mpu -t panic\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/34f9f031-2e2e-41f5-9bad-23cdbee60b93)",
