      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested — Please split this CL** — See the `CL Size \u0026 Scope` section and inline comments below. [[trajectory](https://goto.corp.google.com/traj/34f9f031-2e2e-41f5-9bad-23cdbee60b93)]\n\n### Review Summary\n\n- **Functionality**: `system_disable_jump()` now configures and enables the MPU even when `system_is_locked()` is false, while gating sticky `ram_lock_config_lock_region()` calls on `system_is_locked()` and disabling the MPU in `HOOK_SYSJUMP` so unlocked systems can sysjump cleanly. Additionally, `mpu_protect_code_ram()` configures a 256 MB lower-priority `MPU_ATTR_XN | MPU_ATTR_NO_NO` region (`REGION_CODE_RAM` / `REGION_CODE_RAM2`) under `REGION_STORAGE` when `CONFIG_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` is enabled.\n- **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit**: Gating sticky `ram_lock` hardware configuration inside `mpu_protect_data_ram()` and `mpu_protect_code_ram()` while allowing `system_disable_jump()` to unconditionally configure the MPU fits cleanly with the existing Cortex-M MPU lifecycle (`mpu_pre_init()` -\u003e `HOOK_SYSJUMP` -\u003e `system_disable_jump()`).\n- **Code Simplicity**: The control flow in `common/system.c` and `core/cortex-m/mpu.c` is straightforward, and using `IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_EXTERNAL_STORAGE)` and `IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ROLLBACK_MPU_PROTECT)` avoids additional `#ifdef` nesting.\n- **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability**: In `core/cortex-m/mpu.c` (lines 327–331) and `test/system.c` (lines 89–131), replace bare numeric literals (`28` for the 256 MB code RAM aperture bit-width, plus raw register/address literals in `test/system.c`) with named constants and expressions.\n- **Security**: Keeping the MPU enabled on unlocked systems and marking unused code SRAM in the 256 MB aperture as `MPU_ATTR_XN | MPU_ATTR_NO_NO` strengthens defense-in-depth without locking out developer sysjumps when write-protect is disabled.\n- **Testing**: `test/system.c` adds host unit test coverage for `system_disable_jump()` and `HOOK_SYS