      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Avoid using the bare literal `28` twice for the 256 MB ($2^{28}$-byte) Cortex-M code RAM aperture bit width. Defining a named constant (for example alongside `MPU_SIZE_BITS_MIN` in `core/cortex-m/include/mpu.h` or at the top of `core/cortex-m/mpu.c`) makes the hardware aperture size self-documenting and ensures the base alignment and region size bit-width stay in sync:\n\n```c\n#define MPU_CODE_RAM_APERTURE_BITS 28\n```\n\n```c\n\treturn mpu_update_region(\n\t\tIS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ROLLBACK_MPU_PROTECT) ? REGION_CODE_RAM2 :\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t  REGION_CODE_RAM,\n\t\talign_down_to_bits(CONFIG_PROGRAM_MEMORY_BASE,\n\t\t\t\t   MPU_CODE_RAM_APERTURE_BITS),\n\t\tMPU_CODE_RAM_APERTURE_BITS,\n\t\tMPU_ATTR_XN | MPU_ATTR_NO_NO | MPU_ATTR_INTERNAL_SRAM, 1, 0);\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/34f9f031-2e2e-41f5-9bad-23cdbee60b93)",
