      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] The assertions in `test_mpu_when_unlocked()` only check individual bits of `mock_mpu_size_attr` and omit several key properties and branches:\n\n1. **Access permissions (`MPU_ATTR_NO_NO` / `MPU_ATTR_RO_NO`) and size/subregion fields are not verified:**\n   - Because `MPU_ATTR_NO_NO` is `0 \u003c\u003c 8`, `TEST_BITS_SET(mock_mpu_size_attr[REGION_CODE_RAM] \u003e\u003e 16, MPU_ATTR_XN)` would still pass even if `REGION_CODE_RAM` were configured with `MPU_ATTR_RW_RW`. Asserting the full `size_attr` (`RASR`) word verifies the access permissions (`MPU_ATTR_NO_NO | MPU_ATTR_INTERNAL_SRAM`), the 28-bit size field, the subregion disable mask (`0`), and the enable bit simultaneously.\n   - Similarly, `REGION_STORAGE` and `REGION_STORAGE2` only check `MPU_ATTR_XN` on `REGION_STORAGE` (omitting `REGION_STORAGE2`, `MPU_ATTR_RO_NO | MPU_ATTR_INTERNAL_SRAM`, the size bit-widths `16` and `18`, and the subregion disable masks `0x7f` and `0xf8`), and `REGION_DATA_RAM` is not asserted at all.\n2. **Magic literals in assertions:**\n   - Replace bare literals (`0x10000000`, `0x10080000`, `16`, `1`, `2`) with named constants or expressions derived from `CONFIG_PROGRAM_MEMORY_BASE`, `MPU_CTRL_ENABLE | MPU_CTRL_PRIVDEFENA`, and an explicit helper macro for formatting expected `RASR` values.\n3. **Missing error-path coverage when `ram_lock_config_lock_region()` fails:**\n   - Testing the locked failure case (`ram_lock_config_lock_region()` returning an error) verifies that `system_disable_jump()` aborts before calling `mpu_enable()`.\n\nFor example:\n\n```c\n#define EXPECTED_MPU_RASR(attr, size_bits, srd) \\\n\t(((uint32_t)(attr) \u003c\u003c 16) | (((size_bits) - 1) \u003c\u003c 1) | ((srd) \u003c\u003c 8) | 1)\n#define CODE_RAM_APERTURE_BITS 28\n#define STORAGE1_SIZE_BITS 16\n#define STORAGE1_SRD 0x7f\n#define STORAGE2_SIZE_BITS 18\n#define STORAGE2_SRD 0xf8\n#define DATA_RAM_SIZE_BITS 17\n#define DATA_RAM_SRD 0x00\n#define EXPECTED_MPU_CTRL (MPU_CTRL_ENABLE | MPU_CTRL_PRIVDEFENA)\n#define EXPECTED_LOCKED_REGION_COUNT 2\n\nstatic int test_mpu_when_unlocked(void)\n{\n\t/* Note: initialize_system() already ran and called mpu_pre_init(). */\n\tTEST_EQ(mock_mpu_ctrl, EXPECTED_MPU_CTRL, \"%d\");\n\n\treset_mpu_Mock();\n\tmock_is_locked \u003d 0;\n\n\t/* This should configure the MPU, but not RAM lock. */\n\tsystem_disable_jump();\n\tTEST_EQ(mock_mpu_ctrl, EXPECTED_MPU_CTRL, \"%d\");\n\tTEST_EQ(mock_ram_lock_calls, 0, \"%d\");\n\n\t/* Verify REGION_DATA_RAM is XN + RW and enabled. */\n\tTEST_EQ(mock_mpu_addr[REGION_DATA_RAM],\n\t\tCONFIG_RAM_BASE | MPU_ADDR_VALID | REGION_DATA_RAM, \"0x%08x\");\n\tTEST_EQ(mock_mpu_size_attr[REGION_DATA_RAM],\n\t\tEXPECTED_MPU_RASR(MPU_ATTR_XN | MPU_ATTR_RW_RW |\n\t\t\t\t\t  MPU_ATTR_INTERNAL_SRAM,\n\t\t\t\t  DATA_RAM_SIZE_BITS, DATA_RAM_SRD),\n\t\t\"0x%08x\");\n\n\t/* Verify REGION_CODE_RAM is XN + NO_NO and covers the 256MB aperture. */\n\tTEST_EQ(mock_mpu_addr[REGION_CODE_RAM],\n\t\talign_down_to_bits(CONFIG_PROGRAM_MEMORY_BASE,\n\t\t\t\t   CODE_RAM_APERTURE_BITS) |\n\t\t\tMPU_ADDR_VALID | REGION_CODE_RAM,\n\t\t\"0x%08x\");\n\tTEST_EQ(mock_mpu_size_attr[REGION_CODE_RAM],\n\t\tEXPECTED_MPU_RASR(MPU_ATTR_XN | MPU_ATTR_NO_NO |\n\t\t\t\t\t  MPU_ATTR_INTERNAL_SRAM,\n\t\t\t\t  CODE_RAM_APERTURE_BITS, 0),\n\t\t\"0x%08x\");\n\n\t/*\n\t * Verify REGION_STORAGE and REGION_STORAGE2 are executable + RO_NO\n\t * and cover [0x10070000..0x10080000) and [0x10080000..0x100b0000).\n\t */\n\tTEST_EQ(mock_mpu_addr[REGION_STORAGE],\n\t\talign_down_to_bits(CONFIG_PROGRAM_MEMORY_BASE,\n\t\t\t\t   STORAGE1_SIZE_BITS) |\n\t\t\tMPU_ADDR_VALID | REGION_STORAGE,\n\t\t\"0x%08x\");\n\tTEST_EQ(mock_mpu_size_attr[REGION_STORAGE],\n\t\tEXPECTED_MPU_RASR(MPU_ATTR_RO_NO | MPU_ATTR_INTERNAL_SRAM,\n\t\t\t\t  STORAGE1_SIZE_BITS, STORAGE1_SRD),\n\t\t\"0x%08x\");\n\tTEST_EQ(mock_mpu_addr[REGION_STORAGE2],\n\t\t(CONFIG_PROGRAM_MEMORY_BASE + (1 \u003c\u003c (STORAGE1_SIZE_BITS - 3))) |\n\t\t\tMPU_ADDR_VALID | REGION_STORAGE2,\n\t\t\"0x%08x\");\n\tTEST_EQ(mock_mpu_size_attr[REGION_STORAGE2],\n\t\tEXPECTED_MPU_RASR(MPU_ATTR_RO_NO | MPU_ATTR_INTERNAL_SRAM,\n\t\t\t\t  STORAGE2_SIZE_BITS, STORAGE2_SRD),\n\t\t\"0x%08x\");\n\n\t/* Hooks for HOOK_SYSJUMP should disable the MPU. */\n\thook_notify(HOOK_SYSJUMP);\n\tTEST_EQ(mock_mpu_ctrl, 0, \"%d\");\n\n\t/* When locked, both MPU and RAM lock should be configured. */\n\treset_mpu_Mock();\n\tmock_is_locked \u003d 1;\n\tsystem_disable_jump();\n\tTEST_EQ(mock_mpu_ctrl, EXPECTED_MPU_CTRL, \"%d\");\n\tTEST_EQ(mock_ram_lock_calls, EXPECTED_LOCKED_REGION_COUNT, \"%d\");\n\n\treturn EC_SUCCESS;\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/34f9f031-2e2e-41f5-9bad-23cdbee60b93)",
